    <node id="Installation, Basics">
      <data key="d0">Installation, Basics</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Installation, Basics is a section within the Allplan user interface guide designed to assist users in understanding the initial setup and foundational operations pertinent to using the Allplan software. This section introduces essential concepts for setting up the software and may have originally encompassed instructions regarding the installation procedures specific to different components, such as the Actionbar.

Despite its intended purpose, various descriptions indicate that Installation, Basics consists of content fragments that have been discarded. These fragments suggest that the section was meant to provide introductory guidance on the Allplan installation process, but did not meet necessary standards of detail and organization.

Specifically, Installation, Basics includes information aimed at helping users navigate the initial configurations required for the Allplan environment. However, the existence of repeated references to its status as discarded content implies that it may not currently serve a functional role within the user resources, as it lacked complete and comprehensive coverage of the topics intended for its guidance role. Therefore, the overall presentation of Installation, Basics reflects a mix of foundational concepts essential for new users and a recognition that the information may not be well-organized or complete due to its archival status.</data>
